# Keep the build context small and reproducible. Anything generated inside the
# image must not be shadowed by a stale copy from the working tree.
# .git is deliberately NOT ignored: the Go toolchain reads it to stamp the
# commit into the binary, which is what makes /v1/version able to say which
# build is running. Losing that stamp is how a stale container hides.
.github

ui/node_modules
ui/.next
ui/out

dist/

# Runtime state, which belongs in the compose volumes rather than the image.
# These patterns are matched against every path copied into the build,
# including the contents of a cross-stage COPY — so a pattern here can delete
# a file the build generated itself. images/ once removed the UI's /images
# page that way. The Dockerfile transfers the frontend as an archive to stay
# out of reach of this, and asserts afterwards that every route survived.
database/
secret/
cert/
images/
iso/
*.db

go-via
